   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "At \\( x = \\frac{3}{4} \\) the series alternates, and since \\( 0 < x < 1 \\) the sizes of its terms decrease to 0, so the alternating series error bound applies.",
         "rule_named": "conditions of the alternating series error bound"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The partial sum stops at \\( n = 3 \\), so the first omitted term is the \\( n = 4 \\) term, of size \\( \\frac{x^{4}}{4} \\) for \\( x > 0 \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99040",
         "rule_named": "first omitted term"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "At \\( x = \\frac{3}{4} \\) that size is \\( \\frac{81}{1024} \\), so \\( \\left|f(\\frac{3}{4}) - S_{3}\\right| \\le \\frac{81}{1024} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
